# Files that must not end up in apps/llmchat/ on the server.
# Used via: rsync --exclude-from=.deployignore
#
# The built artefacts in js/ and css/ MUST be transferred — nothing is
# built on the server.

# dependencies and sources — build inputs, useless at runtime
node_modules/
src/
package.json
package-lock.json
vite.config.js

# linter configuration and caches — they only apply to src/ and lib/ in the
# repository, and .php-cs-fixer.dist.php would even fatal at runtime because
# it requires a vendor/ that is deliberately not shipped
eslint.config.js
psalm.xml
.php-cs-fixer.dist.php
.php-cs-fixer.cache

# Never ship a composer/ directory: its presence switches off Nextcloud's
# generic PSR-4 autoloader (AppManager::registerAutoloading), and without a
# vendor/ next to it the app dies with a fatal error.
composer.json
composer.lock
composer/
vendor/

# sourcemaps — 11 of the 14 MB in js/, only useful with src/ present
*.map

# Screenshots are referenced by URL, so the app store and GitHub fetch them
# from the repository — shipping them would put 350 KB of documentation on
# every installation. img/app.svg must stay: it is the navigation icon.
img/[0-9]-*.png

# release tooling and its output — build/ holds the store tarball plus an
# unpacked copy of the whole app, so leaving it in would deploy a second
# llmchat underneath the first one
build/
build-release.sh
Makefile
.cache/

# repo noise
# CHANGELOG.md stays: the app store parses it out of the release archive.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.deployignore
nextcloud-llm-app-spec.md
